endobj
146 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (Climatic and field condition differences create major challenges when applying tea harvesting machines developed for temperate regions to Sri Lankan plantations. These machines are generally designed for uniform terrain, slower shoot growth, and longer plucking rounds, whereas Sri Lankan tea fields have steep slopes, uneven terrain, dense shoot growth, and shorter plucking cycles. As a result, many imported machines show poor adaptability and cannot maintain accurate selective plucking standards. A major limitation is the inability to distinguish between pluckable shoots and non-pluckable shoots such as Arimbu, banji shoots, and other immature developing shoots, causing machines to harvest both required and non-required material simultaneously. This reduces tea quality, damages future yield potential, increases the inclusion of coarse leaves and stems, and, due to uneven terrain, makes it difficult to maintain a constant cutting height, resulting in inconsistent harvesting performance and increased operator fatigue.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
