151 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 90 0 R
/E (            Mechanical tea harvesting systems have been introduced as a possible solution to reduce labour dependency and increase harvesting productivity. Although these systems improve harvesting speed, many existing machines are unable to satisfy the quality requirements.. The major technical issue is the lack of selective plucking capability. Existing machines cannot properly differentiate between mature pluckable shoots and immature shoots such as Arimbu, active buds, and developing shoots intended for future plucking rounds. Consequently, machines remove both required and non-required shoots together, reducing final tea quality and affecting future yield. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
