/P 96 0 R
/E (A literature review was conducted to study tea harvesting practices, plucking standards, tea shoot characteristics, and existing mechanical harvesting systems. A field visit to the Tea Research Institute \(TRI\) Sub Centre, Rathnapura was carried out to observe manual plucking, machine harvesting operations, tea shoot growth stages, and machine-induced damage to tea bushes.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 96 0 R
/E (Based on literature findings and field observations, major limitations of existing harvesting systems were identified, including non-selective plucking, damage to immature shoots, poor terrain adaptability, and operator fatigue. These findings were used to establish the main design requirements of the proposed system, including selective harvesting capability, lightweight structure, ergonomic operation, and reduced plant damage.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
